Looking at the comment: "If the index range is valid, every bit outside the range [fromIndex, toIndex) remains unchanged after the operation."

The valid range condition for this method is `fromIndex >= 0 && toIndex >= 0 && fromIndex <= toIndex`. "Outside the range [fromIndex, toIndex)" means indices `i` where `i < fromIndex || i >= toIndex` (for nonnegative bit indices). Those bits must equal their old values.

<code>assert (fromIndex >= 0 && toIndex >= 0 && fromIndex <= toIndex) => \forall int i; i >= 0 && (i < fromIndex || i >= toIndex); this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i));</code>
